A failed server tool's result for the model: when the thrown error carries a result under
Symbol.for("tanstack-ai.toolResult") (memory-agent's ToolFailed), use it instead of
{ error: message }, so the model gets { error, cause, detail }. The result stays output-error
and onAfterToolCall still gets ok: false. Redo this patch when @tanstack/ai is upgraded.

diff --git a/dist/esm/activities/chat/tools/tool-calls.js b/dist/esm/activities/chat/tools/tool-calls.js
index 61c8cf2f02637a5908b9df697a607c45accabc1a..31a62a0be0954d3f09a2c561daae46c56bc03e34 100644
--- a/dist/esm/activities/chat/tools/tool-calls.js
+++ b/dist/esm/activities/chat/tools/tool-calls.js
@@ -450,7 +450,7 @@ async function* executeServerTool(toolCall, tool, toolName, input, context, pend
 		await pushResultAndRunAfterHook(results, {
 			toolCallId: toolCall.id,
 			toolName,
-			result: { error: message },
+			result: error?.[Symbol.for("tanstack-ai.toolResult")] ?? { error: message },
 			input,
 			state: "output-error",
 			duration
